  "raw": " being possessed. Credit goes to our new Intern for the research, Elliott Allums and everyone else involved in this piece of entertainment.\n[The Crimson Boit]\n\nTonight’s show was a ‘school year for your ears’ spectacle as well as remembering all of the songs from those years that you had passed yourself off on. Great song selection, hears your favorite bands play your favorite songs in maybe their purest form (how could it be wrong?). We would like to list out some items that came through during the set: Opening acts that were named Jimmy Acuff Twice Tonight also did a breakout number. Jocko Cruise played bass in his house shirt!John Sweet Sir Clutteredness played a solo with piano keys.Tablaboy Big Mike and the Cheesehounds recited lyrics of a 1987 classic, Poor Joe’s World made a minor comeback.Dick Roseman and Bill participated in cheering and singing along ofa 1984 altrock hit called Sc",
